<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amenemhat I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 20th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century-bce">20th century BCE</a> · Also known as Amenemhet I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amenemhat I was the founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s Twelfth Dynasty, reigning for about thirty years from around 1985 BCE. Probably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the same name who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mentuhotep-iv">Mentuhotep IV</a>, he moved the royal residence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a> to a new city, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itjtawy">Itjtawy</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisht">Lisht</a>, and reorganised the provinces. He made his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senusret-i">Senusret I</a> co-regent and was apparently murdered in a palace conspiracy, an event reflected in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/instruction-of-amenemhat">Instruction of Amenemhat</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tale-of-sinuhe">Tale of Sinuhe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amenemhat-i.jpg" alt="Amenemhat I" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amenemhat_I_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
